### IPC Mechanisms — `js/pipe.js`, `js/messageQueue.js`, `js/sharedMemory.js`, `js/semaphore.js`

#### [NEW] [pipe.js](file:///c:/Users/MSI%20PC/Desktop/ACADEMICS/SEMISTERS/SEMISTER%20FOUR/CSE316%20OPERATING%20SYSTEMS/OS%20PROJECT/js/pipe.js)

- `Pipe` class: unidirectional, fixed-size buffer
- `write(data)` / `read()` operations with buffer tracking
- Detects pipe full / pipe empty conditions

#### [NEW] [messageQueue.js](file:///c:/Users/MSI%20PC/Desktop/ACADEMICS/SEMISTERS/SEMISTER%20FOUR/CSE316%20OPERATING%20SYSTEMS/OS%20PROJECT/js/messageQueue.js)

- `MessageQueue` class: FIFO queue with max capacity
- `send(msg)` / `receive()` with priority support
- Detects queue overflow

#### [NEW] [sharedMemory.js](file:///c:/Users/MSI%20PC/Desktop/ACADEMICS/SEMISTERS/SEMISTER%20FOUR/CSE316%20OPERATING%20SYSTEMS/OS%20PROJECT/js/sharedMemory.js)

- `SharedMemory` class: key-value store accessible by multiple processes
- Tracks concurrent read/write access
- Flags race conditions when two processes write simultaneously

#### [NEW] [semaphore.js](file:///c:/Users/MSI%20PC/Desktop/ACADEMICS/SEMISTERS/SEMISTER%20FOUR/CSE316%20OPERATING%20SYSTEMS/OS%20PROJECT/js/semaphore.js)

- `Semaphore` class: `wait()` / `signal()` operations
- Tracks which process holds it, and wait queue
- Used by shared memory to demonstrate synchronization

